add('P216-0001','skew-action calculation omitted','Lemma 5.6.1: coinduced skew module','The displayed formulas define a module over the skew group ring and the map b to (g maps to g b) is an injective module homomorphism.','Check the group multiplication and ring multiplication formulas, then the skew commutation relation; evaluate at the identity to prove injectivity and verify the two equivariance identities for the embedding.','skew group ring|coinduction|injective embedding')
add('P216-0002','Hom action and acyclicity computation omitted','Lemma 5.6.1: coinduced Hom','After the split embedding, the Hom module is a direct summand of a coinduced G-module and hence has zero positive group cohomology.','Give the coordinate isomorphism using the conjugation action u^g(a)=g u(g inverse a), check it intertwines G-actions, and apply the contracting homotopy for coinduced group cochains. Direct summands inherit vanishing.','coinduced Hom|group cohomology|conjugation')
add('P216-0003','general injectivity assertion with proof following','Lemma 5.6.2: forgetting equivariance preserves injectivity','For the stated AB5 abelian category with a coherent exact group action, an injective equivariant object is injective after forgetting the action.','Construct the induction functor as the coproduct of all translates, verify its adjunction to forgetting and its exactness using AB4. Its right adjoint therefore preserves injectives. The paper instead extends the transfinite embedding equivariantly; its successor and limit equivariance must be checked.','forget equivariance|induction adjoint|injective object')
